===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|sv|gmq-osw|[[hus|hūs]]}}, from {{inh|sv|non|hús}}, from {{inh|sv|gem-pro|*hūsą||house}}.

====Noun====
{{sv-noun|n}}

# a [[house]]
#: {{ux|sv|ett rött '''hus'''|a red '''house'''}}
#: {{ux|sv|Conny bor i ett '''hus'''|Conny lives in a '''house'''}}
#: {{ux|sv|Jag gick in i '''huset'''|I went into '''the house'''}}
# a [[house]] (restaurant, casino, theater, etc. – place of public accommodation or entertainment)
#: {{ux|sv|'''Huset''' bjuder|It's on '''the house'''}}
#: {{ux|sv|Det var fullt '''hus''' på premiären|There was a full '''house''' at the premiere}}
# {{lb|sv|politics}} a [[house]]
#: {{ux|sv|'''husets''' talman|the speaker of '''the house''' (of representatives)}}
# a [[house]] ((royal) family)
#: {{ux|sv|'''Huset''' Bernadotte har regerat Sverige sedan 1818|'''The house of''' Bernadotte has ruled Sweden since 1818}}
# {{lb|sv|archaic}} a [[castle]] (several Swedish castles have "hus" in their name)
# {{lb|sv|astrology}} a [[house]] (section of the [[zodiac]])
# {{lb|sv|uncommon}} a [[housing]]
#: {{ux|sv|Skruva loss '''huset''' och kolla åt vilket håll termostaten sitter|Unscrew '''the housing''' and check which way the thermostat is facing}}

